<!-- The screens the Coach knows, and how it recognises each one.

     HOW RESOLUTION WORKS, AND WHY THERE ARE ALMOST NO action_tags HERE
     ==================================================================
     `sidebar_key` names a pb.sidebar.item, and learn.screen._matchers() reads
     that leaf's OWN action_tag / action_xmlid / match_* fields at call time.
     So the Coach resolves the active screen exactly the way pb_sidebar decides
     which leaf to highlight, and the two can never disagree. Re-declaring the
     tags here would create a second copy that drifts the first time a leaf is
     re-pointed.

     `action_tags` is therefore the EXCEPTION, used once: the import wizard is a
     flow, not a destination. It has no sidebar leaf of its own — it opens over
     Import Data — so its tag is the only way to know it is showing.

     suggest_ids are wired per screen in Run A2, once the fourteen intents
     exist. The two dynamic intents are offered everywhere in the meantime,
     because a screen that suggests nothing is a dead end for the person who
     opened the Coach precisely because they did not know what to ask. -->
